  intro={[
    "JIS-standard heavy-duty batteries are the workhorse of commercial vehicles across Asia, the Middle East and Africa. The 'N' series (N150, N200) is built on a thick-plate flooded design with a Pb-Sb (lead-antimony) grid — deliberately chosen over thinner automotive plates to survive the deep cycling and vibration of large diesel engines.",
    "The key difference between the two models is size and output. The N150 (145G51) fits standard heavy-truck trays at 508×222×212mm and delivers 900A CCA. The N200 (190H52) is larger at 520×278×220mm and delivers 1100A CCA for the biggest engines and coldest climates. If your tray will take the N200, it is the stronger choice for demanding duty — but always confirm the footprint and terminal orientation before upgrading.",
    "Both are manufactured by Chengguang Power Tech Co., Ltd. under an IATF 16949 quality system, with per-batch CCA test data and full documentation provided with every shipment."
  ]}
  specNotes={[
    "Cold Cranking Amps (CCA) is measured to JIS D5301 — the current a fully charged 12V battery can deliver for 30 seconds at −15°C while holding at least 7.2V. The N150's 900A and the N200's 1100A describe cold-start power: a higher figure means a stronger, more dependable start on a cold morning.",
    "Reserve Capacity (RC), also to SAE J537, is the number of minutes a fully charged battery can sustain a 25-amp load at 27°C (80°F) before the voltage drops to 10.5V. The N150's 220 minutes and the N200's 320 minutes are your buffer for lights, telematics and other loads when the engine is off — or if the alternator fails on the road.",
    "Capacity is measured at the 20-hour rate (C20). The N150's 135Ah and the N200's 200Ah describe the total energy stored over a slow 20-hour discharge at 25°C — a different measure from the short, high-current burst that CCA describes.",
    "Fit and terminals: both models use JIS type A large taper posts. The N150's 508×222×212mm footprint suits standard heavy-truck trays; the N200 is larger at 520×278×220mm. Confirm tray length, width, height and terminal position before upgrading from N150 to N200."
  ]}
