  faq={[
    { q: "What is the difference between N150 and N200?", a: "The JIS N150 (model 145G51) has 135Ah capacity and 900A CCA; the N200 (model 190H52) is larger with 200Ah and 1100A CCA. Choose based on your engine's CCA requirement and battery tray size." },
    { q: "Are these batteries for 12V or 24V systems?", a: "Each is a 12V battery. Heavy trucks using 24V systems wire two of them in series." },
    { q: "What CCA does a JIS N200 provide?", a: "The 190H52 (N200) provides 1100A CCA (JIS D5301), suited to large diesel engines." },
    { q: "What are the dimensions of the N150 and N200?", a: "The N150 (145G51) measures 508×222×212mm; the N200 (190H52) measures 520×278×220mm. Confirm your battery tray will fit the larger model before upgrading." },
    { q: "Are these batteries maintenance-free?", a: "Heavy-duty JIS models use thick-plate flooded (Pb-Sb) construction, which may require periodic electrolyte checks. AGM versions are available where a maintenance-free option is preferred." },
