    { q: "Why do these batteries use a lead-antimony (Pb-Sb) grid?", a: "Antimony strengthens the positive grid and improves resistance to deep cycling, which suits heavy-duty service. The trade-off is slightly higher water consumption, so these batteries are serviceable. AGM versions are available where maintenance-free operation is preferred." },
